        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0197" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg89"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 3, 1894.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 119.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copy of a
                    letter from the minister of foreign affairs of December 16, 1893, to the dean of
                    the diplomatic corps, and a note from the diplomatic corps of the 19th instant,
                    transmitting the above to the commanding officers of the foreign naval
                    forces.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. L.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>




